{
  "uid": "rs-overview",
  "title": "reward-serve overview",
  "description": "One server on one machine. Panels are ordered the way an incident is actually worked: is it failing, is it slow, is it queueing, is it batching, and how fast is the error budget going.",
  "tags": ["reward-serve", "slo"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": false,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "10s",
  "time": { "from": "now-1h", "to": "now" },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "slo_latency_le",
        "label": "Latency SLI bucket, seconds (measured 2026-08-20)",
        "description": "docs/slo.md section 2: 2 x max forward (282 ms) + MAX_WAIT (10 ms) = 574 ms, rounded up to the 0.750 bucket edge. Measured on a gate-passed box; artifact results/obs_dry_run.json.",
        "type": "constant",
        "hide": 2,
        "query": "0.750",
        "current": { "text": "0.750", "value": "0.750" }
      },
      {
        "name": "slo_latency_target",
        "label": "Latency SLO target",
        "type": "constant",
        "hide": 2,
        "query": "0.99",
        "current": { "text": "0.99", "value": "0.99" }
      },
      {
        "name": "slo_availability_target",
        "label": "Availability SLO target",
        "type": "constant",
        "hide": 2,
        "query": "0.995",
        "current": { "text": "0.995", "value": "0.995" }
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Request rate by status",
      "description": "rs_requests_total is per scored item, not per HTTP request: a Form B request with eight pairs counts eight times. Flat at zero here with traffic arriving means the batcher stopped, not that the clients stopped.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "rs-prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "unit": "reqps", "custom": { "fillOpacity": 10, "lineWidth": 2 } },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (status) (rate(rs_requests_total[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{status}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Error rate (non-ok share) and rejections by reason",
      "description": "The blue line is 1 minus the availability SLI. The stacked lines split it into the two ways this server refuses work: queue_full (offered load above capacity) and deadline_exceeded (the queue drained too slowly to meet the deadline). Which one is moving decides whether you shed load or fix latency.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "rs-prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 0 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "unit": "percentunit", "min": 0, "custom": { "fillOpacity": 10 } },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "1 - (sum(rate(rs_requests_total{status=\"ok\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(rs_requests_total[5m])), 0.001))",
          "legendFormat": "error rate"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (rate(rs_rejected_total[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(rs_requests_total[5m])), 0.001)",
          "legendFormat": "{{reason}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Request latency p50 / p95 / p99",
      "description": "Read off rs_request_latency_seconds, whose buckets are cut for a 20-500 ms service (see reward_serve/obs.py). The dashed threshold is the latency SLI bucket edge. p50 rising with p99 means the whole service slowed; p99 rising alone means a few requests are waiting on a batch they keep missing.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "rs-prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 9, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 8 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": { "lineWidth": 2, "fillOpacity": 0 },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "red", "value": 0.35 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le) (rate(rs_request_latency_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(rs_request_latency_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(rs_request_latency_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99"
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(rs_forward_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95 forward only"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Queue depth and queue wait p95",
      "description": "rs_queue_depth is instantaneous. Depth near QUEUE_DEPTH (256) with 429s on the error panel is saturation. Depth near zero while queue wait sits at MAX_WAIT_MS means the flush timer, not the queue, is what each request is waiting on.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "rs-prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 9, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 8 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "custom": { "fillOpacity": 15 } },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "queue wait p95" },
            "properties": [
              { "id": "unit", "value": "s" },
              { "id": "custom.axisPlacement", "value": "right" }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "rs_queue_depth",
          "legendFormat": "queue depth"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(rs_queue_wait_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "queue wait p95"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "heatmap",
      "title": "Achieved batch size distribution",
      "description": "Buckets 1,2,4,8,16,32,64. Everything sitting in the le=1 bucket means the server is doing no batching at all, whatever the config says, and every forward pass is paying full cost for one item.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "rs-prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 9, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 17 },
      "options": {
        "calculate": false,
        "cellGap": 2,
        "color": { "mode": "scheme", "scheme": "Oranges", "steps": 32 },
        "yAxis": { "unit": "short" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (le) (rate(rs_batch_size_bucket[1m]))",
          "format": "heatmap",
          "legendFormat": "{{le}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Mean achieved batch size",
      "description": "rs_batch_size_sum over rs_batch_size_count. One number to answer whether batching is happening.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "rs-prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 4, "w": 6, "x": 12, "y": 17 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 2,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "red", "value": null },
              { "color": "orange", "value": 1.5 },
              { "color": "green", "value": 3 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(rs_batch_size_sum[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(rs_batch_size_count[5m])), 0.001)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Latency SLI (share under $slo_latency_le s, 30d)",
      "description": "The compliance number the error budget is spent from.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "rs-prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 4, "w": 6, "x": 18, "y": 17 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 4,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "red", "value": null },
              { "color": "green", "value": 0.99 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(rs_request_latency_seconds_bucket{le=\"$slo_latency_le\"}[30d])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(rs_request_latency_seconds_count[30d])), 0.001)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Fast burn: availability, 1h and 5m windows (page at 14.4x)",
      "description": "Burn rate is the observed error ratio divided by the budget ratio. 14.4x on both windows burns a 30-day budget in about two days and is worth waking someone for; the 5m window is what stops a page firing on a burst that already ended.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "rs-prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 26 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": { "lineWidth": 2, "fillOpacity": 5 },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "red", "value": 14.4 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "(1 - (sum(rate(rs_requests_total{status=\"ok\"}[1h])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(rs_requests_total[1h])), 0.001))) / (1 - $slo_availability_target)",
          "legendFormat": "1h burn"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "(1 - (sum(rate(rs_requests_total{status=\"ok\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(rs_requests_total[5m])), 0.001))) / (1 - $slo_availability_target)",
          "legendFormat": "5m burn"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "vector(14.4)",
          "legendFormat": "page threshold"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Slow burn: availability, 6h and 30m windows (ticket at 6x)",
      "description": "The slow pair catches a small, steady leak that never trips the fast alert but still empties the budget inside the window. It raises a ticket, not a page.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "rs-prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 26 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": { "lineWidth": 2, "fillOpacity": 5 },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "orange", "value": 6 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "(1 - (sum(rate(rs_requests_total{status=\"ok\"}[6h])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(rs_requests_total[6h])), 0.001))) / (1 - $slo_availability_target)",
          "legendFormat": "6h burn"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "(1 - (sum(rate(rs_requests_total{status=\"ok\"}[30m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(rs_requests_total[30m])), 0.001))) / (1 - $slo_availability_target)",
          "legendFormat": "30m burn"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "vector(6)",
          "legendFormat": "ticket threshold"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Latency burn: fast (1h/5m) and slow (6h/30m)",
      "description": "The same two-window pattern applied to the latency SLI, so a service that is up but slow still spends a budget and still alerts.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "rs-prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 34 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "unit": "short", "custom": { "lineWidth": 2, "fillOpacity": 5 } },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "(1 - (sum(rate(rs_request_latency_seconds_bucket{le=\"$slo_latency_le\"}[1h])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(rs_request_latency_seconds_count[1h])), 0.001))) / (1 - $slo_latency_target)",
          "legendFormat": "1h latency burn"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "(1 - (sum(rate(rs_request_latency_seconds_bucket{le=\"$slo_latency_le\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(rs_request_latency_seconds_count[5m])), 0.001))) / (1 - $slo_latency_target)",
          "legendFormat": "5m latency burn"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "(1 - (sum(rate(rs_request_latency_seconds_bucket{le=\"$slo_latency_le\"}[6h])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(rs_request_latency_seconds_count[6h])), 0.001))) / (1 - $slo_latency_target)",
          "legendFormat": "6h latency burn"
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "(1 - (sum(rate(rs_request_latency_seconds_bucket{le=\"$slo_latency_le\"}[30m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(rs_request_latency_seconds_count[30m])), 0.001))) / (1 - $slo_latency_target)",
          "legendFormat": "30m latency burn"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
